[1mThe one real mismatch: [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m.[22m When stdout is a pipe with no reader, the C program is killed by signal 13 (shell status 141) but the Rust program exited 0. The Rust standard library installs [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m runs, so the write returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m instead of raising a fatal signal — and [38;5;10mmain[0m discarded that error along with all other write errors. stdout and stderr were byte-identical in both cases, so this is precisely the failure a stdout-only assertion would have missed. Fixed by restoring [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m as the first action in [38;5;10mmain[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
